        "english": "Some trees are like my venerable grandfather,\nBearing only sparse, weathered leaves upon their crown!\nSome trees are gentle like my grandmother,\nCrumbling sweet bread to feed the morning crows!\nOne tree is tender like my beloved—\nA sweet, fragrant sapling of mango!\nAnd some young saplings my heart yearns\nTo hoist upon my shoulders and bounce in play!",
