    "philosophyTheme": "mortality",
    "landscapeBiome": "cremation_dusk",
    "sketchPrompt": "Fine pencil sketch of autumn leaves detaching from a branch and spiraling downward toward a dark, undisturbed pool of water.",
    "historicalFact": {
      "claim": "The title poem sequence of the posthumous collection 'Alvida', which Guru Nanak Dev University scholar Satinder Singh cited as Shiv's conscious surrender to fate.",
      "citationId": "SINGH-1983-HERITAGE"
    },
    "summary": "A dignified, solemn severance of ties with earthly existence, forgiving the world for its cruelty and choosing eternal quietude.",
    "backstory": "Representing the culmination of Shiv's lifelong preoccupation with early departure, executed with tender equanimity.",
    "stanzas": [
      {
        "gurmukhi": "ਜ਼ਿੰਦਗੀ ਤੈਨੂੰ ਅਲਵਿਦਾ ਕਹਿੰਦੇ ਹਾਂ,\nਤੇਰੇ ਸ਼ਹਿਰੋਂ ਹੁਣ ਤੁਰ ਚੱਲੇ ਹਾਂ!\nਜਿੰਨੇ ਜ਼ਖ਼ਮ ਤੂੰ ਦਿੱਤੇ ਸੀ ਸਾਨੂੰ,\nਅਸੀਂ ਸੀਨੇ ਲਾ ਕੇ ਖੱਲੇ ਹਾਂ!",
        "shahmukhi": "زندگی تینوں الوداع کہندے ہاں،\nتیرے شہروں ہن تر چلے ہاں!\nجنے زخم توں دتے سی سانوں،\nاسیں سینے لا کے کھلے ہاں!",
        "roman": "Zindagi tainu alvida kehnde haan,\nTere shehron hun tur challe haan!\nJinne zakham tu ditte si saanu,\nAseen seene laa ke khalle haan!",
        "english": "To you, mortal life, we bid our solemn farewell;\nWe pack our grief and depart from your cruel city!\nEvery deep wound that you mercilessly dealt against our soul\nWe have pressed to our breast and endured in lonely silence!",
        "commentary": "Acceptance without bitterness; wounded pride transmuted into dignified farewell."
      },
      {
        "gurmukhi": "ਨਾ ਕੋਈ ਸ਼ਿਕਵਾ ਨਾ ਕੋਈ ਰੋਸਾ,\nਨਾ ਕਿਸੇ ਨਾਲ਼ ਕੋਈ ਵੈਰ ਨੀ!\nਜਿਸ ਰਾਹ ਉੱਤੇ ਮੌਤ ਖਲੋਤੀ,\nਉਸ ਰਾਹ ਪਾ ਲਏ ਪੈਰ ਨੀ!",
        "shahmukhi": "نہ کوئی شکوہ نہ کوئی روسا،\nنہ کسے نال کوئی ویر نی!\nجس راہ اتے موت کھلوتی،\nاس راہ پا لئے پیر نی!",
        "roman": "Na koi shikwa na koi rosa,\nNa kise naal koi vair ni!\nJis raah utte maut khaloti,\nUss raah paa laye pair ni!",
        "english": "No grievance lingers in our heart, no sullen grudge remains;\nNot a trace of enmity do we bear against any living soul!\nUpon that path where Death stands waiting like a patient bride,\nWe have set our weary feet without hesitation or fear!",
        "commentary": "Death framed not as an executioner, but as a peaceful sanctuary."
      },
      {
        "gurmukhi": "ਖ਼ੁਸ਼ ਰਹਿਣ ਇਹ ਵੱਸਦੇ ਲੋਕੀਂ,\nਖ਼ੁਸ਼ ਰਹਿਣ ਇਹ ਮਹਿਲਾਂ ਵਾਲ਼ੇ!\nਸ਼ਿਵ ਤਾਂ ਚੱਲਿਆ ਸਿਵਿਆਂ ਵੱਲ ਨੂੰ,\nਜਿੱਥੇ ਚਾਨਣ ਕਰਦੇ ਛਾਲ਼ੇ!",
        "shahmukhi": "خوش رہن ایہ وسدے لوکی،\nخوش رہن ایہ محلاں والے!\nشیو تاں چلیا سویاں ول نوں،\nجتھے چانن کردے چھالے!",
        "roman": "Khush rehan eh vassde lokin,\nKhush rehan eh mehlaan waale!\nShiv taan chaleya siveyaan vall nu,\nJitthe chanan karde chhaale!",
        "english": "May these thriving multitudes dwell forever in merriment!\nMay the dwellers of grand palaces flourish in prosperity!\nAs for Shiv, he has turned his face toward the cremation ground,\nWhere the blisters of his weeping heart provide their own radiant light!",
        "commentary": "Ironic blessing for worldly vanity contrasted with the sacred light of the cremation ground (*siveyaan*)."
      }
    ],
